{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A9suopLfVmTKzzUWBP6eVx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.0-uc004-fold\n     2→title: \"Wrap long lines to a fixed width via fold\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go fold binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary wraps\n     6→  lines that exceed the maximum width by inserting newlines at the specified column or\n     7→  byte boundary, optionally breaking at word boundaries. The differential testing harness\n     8→  then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gfold from coreutils)\n     9→  with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd023-fold.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/fold.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go fold binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: printf 'abcdefghijklmnop' | ./bin/fold -w 4\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/fold reads the input line by line. For each line, it measures the width (column\n    25→      positions by default, byte count with -b) and inserts a newline after every W units.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      When -s is active, cmd/fold scans each segment for the last space at or before the\n    29→      wrap column and breaks there instead of at the hard column position.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/fold and gfold\n    33→      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    37→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    38→  - id: F6\n    39→    step: |\n    40→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    41→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    42→\n    43→touchpoints:\n    44→  - T1: \"cmd/fold — line width measurement, newline insertion, tab column expansion, space-break mode (prd023-fold R1, R2, R3)\"\n    45→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    46→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    47→\n    48→success_criteria:\n    49→  - id: S1\n    50→    criterion: cmd/fold compiles and ./bin/fold exists after mage build.\n    51→  - id: S2\n    52→    criterion: The differential test for default width (80) passes; lines exceeding 80 columns are wrapped.\n    53→  - id: S3\n    54→    criterion: The differential test for -w 4 passes; lines are split every 4 columns, matching gfold.\n    55→  - id: S4\n    56→    criterion: The differential test for -w N -s passes; lines break at the last space within N columns.\n    57→  - id: S5\n    58→    criterion: The differential test for -b passes; width is measured in bytes, not columns.\n    59→  - id: S6\n    60→    criterion: The differential test for tab-containing input passes; tabs expand to the correct column positions for wrap-point calculation.\n    61→  - id: S7\n    62→    criterion: A line shorter than the width passes through unchanged.\n    63→\n    64→out_of_scope:\n    65→  - Unicode multi-byte grapheme width calculation is not implemented; LC_ALL=C single-byte behavior is the requirement.\n    66→  - Lines without a trailing newline are handled by matching GNU behavior exactly.\n    67→\n    68→test_suite: test-rel05.0\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab279970-93cc-4d72-a577-0214f24f20cf","uuid":"9b23c8a9-30eb-4b26-a58a-d5abeb305d1e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/349/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.0-uc004-fold.yaml","content":"id: rel05.0-uc004-fold\ntitle: \"Wrap long lines to a fixed width via fold\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go fold binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary wraps\n  lines that exceed the maximum width by inserting newlines at the specified column or\n  byte boundary, optionally breaking at word boundaries. The differential testing harness\n  then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gfold from coreutils)\n  with identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd023-fold.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/fold.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go fold binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf 'abcdefghijklmnop' | ./bin/fold -w 4\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/fold reads the input line by line. For each line, it measures the width (column\n      positions by default, byte count with -b) and inserts a newline after every W units.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      When -s is active, cmd/fold scans each segment for the last space at or before the\n      wrap column and breaks there instead of at the hard column position.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/fold and gfold\n      with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/fold — line width measurement, newline insertion, tab column expansion, space-break mode (prd023-fold R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/fold compiles and ./bin/fold exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for default width (80) passes; lines exceeding 80 columns are wrapped.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -w 4 passes; lines are split every 4 columns, matching gfold.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for -w N -s passes; lines break at the last space within N columns.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -b passes; width is measured in bytes, not columns.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for tab-containing input passes; tabs expand to the correct column positions for wrap-point calculation.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: A line shorter than the width passes through unchanged.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Unicode multi-byte grapheme width calculation is not implemented; LC_ALL=C single-byte behavior is the requirement.\n  - Lines without a trailing newline are handled by matching GNU behavior exactly.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.0\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
