{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012TdsrVN9AV8ELEu6CbF3ZY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/349/cmd/fold/main.go has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab279970-93cc-4d72-a577-0214f24f20cf","uuid":"ed41e302-0a67-40dc-8497-f2f39174da0c","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/349/cmd/fold/main.go","oldString":"\t\tif col == width {\n\t\t\t// Exactly at the width boundary.\n\t\t\tif spaceBreak && lastSpace >= 0 {\n\t\t\t\treturn lastSpace + 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn i + 1\n\t\t}","newString":"\t\tif col == width {\n\t\t\t// Exactly at the width boundary — hard break here.\n\t\t\treturn i + 1\n\t\t}","originalFile":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// Package main implements the fold utility (prd023-fold R1-R4).\n// fold wraps each input line to fit a specified width (default 80 columns),\n// reading from files or stdin, with optional byte-mode (-b) and\n// word-boundary breaking (-s).\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"bufio\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\n// tabStop is the column interval for tab stops.\nconst tabStop = 8\n\nfunc main() {\n\t// R4.4: Handle SIGPIPE gracefully.\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\twidth := 80\n\tbyteMode := false\n\tspaceBreak := false\n\n\targs := os.Args[1:]\n\tvar files []string\n\n\t// Manual flag parsing to match GNU fold behavior.\n\ti := 0\n\tfor i < len(args) {\n\t\targ := args[i]\n\t\tif arg == \"--\" {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, args[i+1:]...)\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(arg) == 0 || arg[0] != '-' || arg == \"-\" {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// Parse flags from the argument.\n\t\tj := 1\n\t\tfor j < len(arg) {\n\t\t\tswitch arg[j] {\n\t\t\tcase 'b':\n\t\t\t\tbyteMode = true\n\t\t\t\tj++\n\t\t\tcase 's':\n\t\t\t\tspaceBreak = true\n\t\t\t\tj++\n\t\t\tcase 'w':\n\t\t\t\t// R2.1: -w N sets width.\n\t\t\t\tval := arg[j+1:]\n\t\t\t\tif val == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\t\ti++\n\t\t\t\t\tif i < len(args) {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tval = args[i]\n\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\tn, err := strconv.Atoi(val)\n\t\t\t\tif err != nil || n <= 0 {\n\t\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"fold: invalid number of columns: '%s'\\n\", val)\n\t\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\twidth = n\n\t\t\t\tj = len(arg) // consumed rest of arg\n\t\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"fold: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", arg[j])\n\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\ti++\n\t}\n\n\t// R1.1: Read stdin when no file arguments are given.\n\tif len(files) == 0 {\n\t\tfiles = []string{\"-\"}\n\t}\n\n\texitCode := 0\n\tw := bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)\n\n\tfor _, file := range files {\n\t\tr, err := openInput(file)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"fold: %v\\n\", err)\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif err := foldInput(r, w, width, byteMode, spaceBreak); err != nil {\n\t\t\t// R4.3: Exit 1 on write error.\n\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif closer, ok := r.(io.Closer); ok && file != \"-\" {\n\t\t\tcloser.Close() // best-effort close\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tif err := w.Flush(); err != nil {\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n}\n\n// openInput returns a reader for the named file, or stdin if name is \"-\".\nfunc openInput(name string) (io.Reader, error) {\n\tif name == \"-\" {\n\t\treturn os.Stdin, nil\n\t}\n\treturn os.Open(name)\n}\n\n// foldInput reads from r and writes folded output to w.\nfunc foldInput(r io.Reader, w *bufio.Writer, width int, byteMode, spaceBreak bool) error {\n\tbr := bufio.NewReader(r)\n\tfor {\n\t\tline, err := readLine(br)\n\t\tif len(line) > 0 {\n\t\t\tif writeErr := foldLine(w, line, width, byteMode, spaceBreak); writeErr != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn writeErr\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tif err == io.EOF {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// readLine reads a single line from the reader, including the trailing newline if present.\n// Returns the line bytes and any error.\nfunc readLine(r *bufio.Reader) ([]byte, error) {\n\tvar line []byte\n\tfor {\n\t\tchunk, isPrefix, err := r.ReadLine()\n\t\tline = append(line, chunk...)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn line, err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !isPrefix {\n\t\t\t// ReadLine strips the newline; add it back.\n\t\t\tline = append(line, '\\n')\n\t\t\treturn line, nil\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// foldLine wraps a single line (which may end with '\\n') and writes it to w.\nfunc foldLine(w *bufio.Writer, line []byte, width int, byteMode, spaceBreak bool) error {\n\t// R1.4: Detect and preserve (or not) trailing newline.\n\thasNewline := len(line) > 0 && line[len(line)-1] == '\\n'\n\tcontent := line\n\tif hasNewline {\n\t\tcontent = line[:len(line)-1]\n\t}\n\n\tfor len(content) > 0 {\n\t\t// Measure the segment up to width units.\n\t\tbreakPos := findBreakPos(content, width, byteMode, spaceBreak)\n\n\t\tif breakPos >= len(content) {\n\t\t\t// R1.2: Remaining content fits; write it and the trailing newline if any.\n\t\t\tif _, err := w.Write(content); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif hasNewline {\n\t\t\t\tif err := w.WriteByte('\\n'); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// R1.3: Write the segment and insert a newline.\n\t\tif _, err := w.Write(content[:breakPos]); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := w.WriteByte('\\n'); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tcontent = content[breakPos:]\n\t}\n\n\t// Empty content but had a newline.\n\tif hasNewline {\n\t\tif err := w.WriteByte('\\n'); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// findBreakPos determines where to break content, returning the byte index.\nfunc findBreakPos(content []byte, width int, byteMode, spaceBreak bool) int {\n\tif byteMode {\n\t\treturn findBreakByte(content, width, spaceBreak)\n\t}\n\treturn findBreakColumn(content, width, spaceBreak)\n}\n\n// findBreakByte finds the break position using byte counting.\nfunc findBreakByte(content []byte, width int, spaceBreak bool) int {\n\tif len(content) <= width {\n\t\treturn len(content)\n\t}\n\n\tbreakAt := width\n\n\tif spaceBreak {\n\t\t// R3.1: Find the last space at or before the width.\n\t\tlastSpace := -1\n\t\tfor i := 0; i < width; i++ {\n\t\t\tif content[i] == ' ' {\n\t\t\t\tlastSpace = i\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\t// R3.3: Break after the space character.\n\t\tif lastSpace >= 0 {\n\t\t\tbreakAt = lastSpace + 1\n\t\t}\n\t\t// R3.2: If no space found, fall back to hard break at width.\n\t}\n\n\treturn breakAt\n}\n\n// findBreakColumn finds the break position using column counting with tab expansion.\nfunc findBreakColumn(content []byte, width int, spaceBreak bool) int {\n\tcol := 0\n\tlastSpace := -1\n\n\tfor i := 0; i < len(content); i++ {\n\t\tch := content[i]\n\n\t\tvar newCol int\n\t\tif ch == '\\t' {\n\t\t\t// R2.2: Tab expands to next tab stop.\n\t\t\tnewCol = col + (tabStop - col%tabStop)\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tnewCol = col + 1\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif newCol > width {\n\t\t\t// This character pushes past the width.\n\t\t\tif spaceBreak && lastSpace >= 0 {\n\t\t\t\treturn lastSpace + 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn i\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif ch == ' ' {\n\t\t\tlastSpace = i\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tcol = newCol\n\n\t\tif col == width {\n\t\t\t// Exactly at the width boundary.\n\t\t\tif spaceBreak && lastSpace >= 0 {\n\t\t\t\treturn lastSpace + 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn i + 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn len(content)\n}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":267,"oldLines":10,"newStart":267,"newLines":7,"lines":["     col = newCol"," ","     if col == width {","-      // Exactly at the width boundary.","-      if spaceBreak && lastSpace >= 0 {","-        return lastSpace + 1","-      }","+      // Exactly at the width boundary — hard break here.","       return i + 1","     }","   }"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01H8kB83NLtJ75vRairqhZAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, but that's wrong too. Consider: \"abcde fghijk\" with -w 11 -s. At column 11, if position 10 is 'k', then we'd hard-break after 'k'. But if position 5 has a space, shouldn't -s prefer to break there? Actually no — if the segment is exactly 11 columns, there's no need to break at all if the content ends there. But if there's more content after, we need to break at column 11.\n\nHmm, let me think about this differently. The `col == width` case means the current character filled the last column. If there are more characters, we need to break. With -s, should we prefer the space?\n\nThe test says \"hello world foo\\n\" with -w 11 should produce \"hello world\\nfoo\\n\". \"hello world\" is 11 chars filling exactly 11 columns. The break is at position 11 (after 'd'). The space at position 5 is NOT used. So `col == width` → hard break at `i+1`, regardless of -s.\n\nBut wait, what about \"hello world foo\" with -w 6 -s? \"hello \" is 6 chars. The space is at position 5, col 6 after space = exactly width. We'd return 6 (i+1 where i=5), which puts \"hello \" on the first line. That seems correct.\n\nWhat about \"abcde fg\" with -w 5 -s? At position 4 ('e'), col=5=width → return 5. Output: \"abcde\\n fg\". But with -s, maybe we should break at some space? There's no space in the first 5 chars, so no issue.\n\nWhat about \"ab cd efg\" with -w 5 -s? \n- i=0 'a' col=1, i=1 'b' col=2, i=2 ' ' col=3 lastSpace=2, i=3 'c' col=4, i=4 'd' col=5=width → return 5.\nOutput: \"ab cd\\n efg\". Hmm, is that right? With -s at width 5, the last space is at position 2. Should we break after position 2 to get \"ab \\ncd efg\"? \n\nLet me test with BSD fold:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":371,"cache_read_input_tokens":79083,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":371},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab279970-93cc-4d72-a577-0214f24f20cf","uuid":"d775fe05-af1b-4cfa-907a-51e68a8d098d"}
